<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's BNDES to inject 1.6 bn reais in telecoms.</title>
<headline>Brazil's BNDES to inject 1.6 bn reais in telecoms.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's National Development Bank (BNDES) and federal giant Telebras signed deal to inject 1.6 billion reais ($1.49 billion) in the telecom's 28 state-level units via a capital hike, a local newspaper said.</p>
<p>Financial daily Gazeta Mercantil, quoting bank President Luis Carlos Mendonca de Barros, said Telebras will grant the BNDES share subscription rights with a 110 million-real premium and the bank will inject 1.6 billion reais by buying shares.</p>
<p>The money will be used to prepare Brazil's state-dominated telecoms sector for privatization, pay cash for share subscription rights and boost investments to expand the country's telephone network, the paper said.</p>
<p>((--James Craig, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 2485413))</p>
